armacraft perf patch 0002 -- UNAPPLIED. Render memo + generation sweep (server-thread O(walls) -> O(changed)).

Why: ArenaRenderer.render rebuilds every wall's piece specs every tick (WallLayout.pieces, key strings,
WallLayout.transform, DyePalette.closest = 17 HSV conversions with trig per wall), rebuilds the rim
specs every tick, and each EntitySet.sync runs Reconcile.diff, which copies both key sets into
LinkedHashSets and builds add/keep/remove sets. Only head walls (one per alive cycle) and walls that
got new holes actually change between ticks.

What it does:
- per reconciliation key (WallKeys), memoise the wall record + owner colour and the piece keys/specs
  built from it; unchanged walls reuse the same spec instances;
- colour -> dye name cached per packed RGB; rim specs built once per round (and on layout change);
- EntitySet gets begin()/want()/end(): a generation sweep replaces Reconcile.diff, and want()
  short-circuits on spec identity before calling equals(). sync(map) still works (wraps the three).
  rekeyPrefix is kept as is.
Output (entities, keys, update calls) is the same as before; a layout/config change drops the memo.

Effect (measured with tools/bench/HostTickBench, a line-by-line mirror without Minecraft types, see
docs/perf.md): per-tick server-thread time 0.64 -> 0.09 ms and allocation 475 -> 76 KB on the largest
captured 32-AI frame; 6.4 -> 1.0 ms at 3000 walls, 27 -> 5.6 ms at 10000 (synthetic).
Base: render/ArenaRenderer.java + render/EntitySet.java as of 2026-10-02 00:08 BST (with WallKeys).
Checked: `git apply --check`; host main + test + gametest sources compile; the 60 host unit tests pass
with 0001+0002+0004 applied (scratch copy, JUnit launcher); the bench mirror of this pipeline ends
each tick with the same number of tracked wall entities as the current one. Not run in a server.
Apply from the repo root:  git apply docs/perf-patches/0002-host-render-memo.patch

